  "review_comments": [
    {
      "id": 4051556159,
      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Traverse ambient TypeScript declarations**\n\nHandle `ambient_declaration` wrappers and `function_signature` nodes before collecting symbols. Common TypeScript declaration syntax such as `declare function load(): void` and `export declare class Service {}` is nested under an ambient declaration, but this loop only unwraps one `export_statement` layer and therefore reports the file as parsed while silently omitting its top-level named functions or classes.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
    },
    {
      "id": 4051556170,
      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Resolve extensionless imports whose basename contains a dot**\n\nTreat a suffix as explicit only when it is one of the supported source extensions. For a unique captured file such as `lib/widget.test.ts`, the valid relative import `./widget.test` produces `base == 'lib/widget.test'`; `splitext` sees `.test`, so no `.ts` candidate is generated and the edge is incorrectly stored as an external module instead of the local component.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
    }
  ],
  "review_resolution": "Both findings reproduced before correction; ambient/signature and dotted imports regressions PASS. No unaddressed new review IDs.",
